16. ChartVolt design system
Use the actual provided ChartVolt background and transparent neon icon assets; do not create a new unrelated page theme. Dark navy glass surfaces, restrained cyan border/blue glow, gold for money/CTA, purple for awards, green for live/success, amber for pending, red for cancelled/warning. The existing glossy neon CTA style remains; use it with readable text and adequate padding. Important surfaces glow; every text tile should not.
Suggested type sizes: title 20–24px, section heading 16–18px, body 13–15px, stat value 18–23px, stat label 11–13px, CTA 15–17px. Respect accessible contrast and line-height. Keep darkened background behind textual content; the dramatic neon stadium environment is atmospheric, not a competing text background.
Avoid fixed heights for text-bearing cards. Use `height: auto`, grid/flex min-width rules, and dynamic growth. The user must be able to read titles and complete key values without tapping extra controls.
