18. Safe area, browser overlays, and accessibility
Avoid nesting a new full-height scroll container inside Safari's existing page scroll. On iPhone Safari, toolbars expand/collapse; sticky UI must not overlap the action or interfere with scroll. Reuse the app shell's safe-area inset handling rather than double-applying it. If navigation is fixed, content bottom spacing must account for both nav height and `env(safe-area-inset-bottom)`. Scroll-to-tab anchors require `scroll-margin-top` when a fixed header is present.
Accessible headings, `aria-live` for important state changes (not every ticking second), clear focus rings, reduced-motion support, 44px targets, real button/links, keyboard-operable tabs, alt text and sufficient contrast.
19. Loading, empty, errors, and performance
Use section-accurate skeletons for hero, metric tiles, action area and details. If leaderboard data is empty, show a purposeful empty state without hiding registration. If one noncritical module fails, show inline Retry instead of crashing the entire lobby. Never show a false `Reserve Spot` CTA while eligibility is unresolved. Use optimized mobile images and priority-load the visible hero; lazy-load sections and imagery below the fold. Cache where existing architecture supports it. Avoid constant re-rendering of every panel due to a per-second countdown.
